Yeah.
是的。

00:42:01.219 --> 00:42:28.579
I mean, in some ways, like when we read novels as teenagers or in your 20s before you've experienced loss, it's all intellectual, you know, and it's hard to, I think one of the big things of how I met your mother is life will season you, life will, you'll trip enough, you'll get left at enough altars, you'll, you know, your plans will be thwarted enough.
我的意思是，在某些方面，就像我们在十几岁的时候或在你经历过失去之前的20多岁的时候读小说一样，这都是智力上的，你知道，而且很难，我认为我遇见你母亲的最重要的事情之一就是生活会磨练你，生活会，你会绊倒足够多的人，你会被留在足够多的祭坛上，你会，你知道，你的计划将受到足够的挫败。

00:42:28.579 --> 00:42:43.219
Yeah, I think that if you let life, if you agree that life is a benevolent teacher, but it's sometimes a ferocious teacher, it really does teach you all the deepest lessons that you could possibly learn.
是的，我认为，如果你让生活，如果你同意生活是一位仁慈的老师，但有时它也是一位凶猛的老师，它确实会教给你所有你可能学到的最深刻的教训。

00:42:43.219 --> 00:42:53.561
Now, I wish that life taught us through success and triumph and, you know, like, it just doesn't seem like the deepest lessons come from those things.
现在，我希望生活能通过成功和胜利教会我们，你知道，这些事情似乎并没有给我们带来最深刻的教训。

00:42:53.561 --> 00:43:00.179
